707
01:17:35,359 --> 01:17:36,360
Jerome Morrow.

708
01:17:46,620 --> 01:17:48,038
You don't look well, Jerome.

709
01:17:49,832 --> 01:17:51,416
Why don't you go home?

710
01:18:02,803 --> 01:18:05,264
- Can I help you?
- I'm looking for Jerome Morrow.

711
01:18:05,806 --> 01:18:09,100
I'm sorry, he's ill. A little nausea.
It's quite common before a mission.

712
01:18:09,184 --> 01:18:10,185
Really?

713
01:18:11,436 --> 01:18:14,636
I ought to pay him a visit.
I understand you can show me the way.

714
01:19:00,360 --> 01:19:02,360
You don't know who he is, do you, Irene?

715
01:19:22,424 --> 01:19:23,883
- Hello?
- Eugene.

716
01:19:23,967 --> 01:19:25,867
I need you to be yourself for the day.

717
01:19:26,303 --> 01:19:29,681
- I was never very good at it, remember?
- The investigators are coming by.

718
01:19:29,765 --> 01:19:32,726
- I'm supposed to be sick.
- So you keep telling me.

719
01:19:33,268 --> 01:19:35,312
- How long have I got?
<i>- Not long.</i>

720
01:21:24,421 --> 01:21:25,756
I guess he's not home.

721
01:21:29,217 --> 01:21:31,595
<i>- Hello?</i>
- I'm here to see Jerome Morrow.

722
01:21:31,928 --> 01:21:33,472
Yes, that's me. Come up.

723
01:21:35,307 --> 01:21:36,683
I guess he's home.

724
01:22:12,469 --> 01:22:13,553
Come in.

725
01:22:16,431 --> 01:22:17,307
Come in.

726
01:22:20,185 --> 01:22:21,228
Hello, sweetheart.

727
01:22:25,190 --> 01:22:26,274
Where's my kiss?

728
01:22:30,487 --> 01:22:32,187
Good to see you're feeling better.

729
01:22:34,199 --> 01:22:36,701
Of course, now that you're here.

730
01:22:46,169 --> 01:22:47,170
Who's your friend?

731
01:22:49,131 --> 01:22:50,382
How can I help?

732
01:22:51,299 --> 01:22:52,499
It's about the director.

733
01:22:54,636 --> 01:22:55,470
Again?

734
01:22:55,554 --> 01:22:58,014
- I hope it's no trouble.
- No, no. No trouble.

735
01:22:59,808 --> 01:23:01,958
Forgive me for not giving you
a guided tour.

736
01:23:02,352 --> 01:23:03,852
Can't we do this another time?

737
01:23:04,479 --> 01:23:07,899
- This won't take a moment.
- Maybe he can tell me what I've got.

738
01:23:45,812 --> 01:23:46,980
Who were you expecting?

739
01:24:31,066 --> 01:24:32,275
- Yes.
<i>- We have our man, sir.</i>

740
01:24:32,359 --> 01:24:33,860
- You have him?
<i>- In custody.</i>

741
01:24:33,944 --> 01:24:35,028
I'll come right away.

742
01:25:00,053 --> 01:25:01,179
How are you, Jerome?

743
01:25:02,764 --> 01:25:03,848
Not bad, Jerome.

744
01:25:07,060 --> 01:25:08,710
How the hell did you get up here?

745
01:25:09,020 --> 01:25:12,565
Oh, I could always walk.
I've been faking it.

746
01:25:28,957 --> 01:25:29,833
Irene.

747
01:25:30,417 --> 01:25:32,043
Irene. Irene.

748
01:25:32,127 --> 01:25:34,296
- Don't touch me.
- Listen to me, Irene.

749
01:25:34,629 --> 01:25:35,963
I don't even know who you are.

750
01:25:36,047 --> 01:25:38,091
I'm the same person I was yesterday.

751
01:25:39,217 --> 01:25:41,177
I can't hear any more
of your lies, Jerome.

752
01:25:41,261 --> 01:25:44,972
My name is Vincent.
All right? Vincent Anton Freeman.

753
01:25:45,056 --> 01:25:48,684
And I'm a faith birth, or a de-gene-erate,
whatever you want to call it.

754
01:25:48,768 --> 01:25:50,353
But I am not a murderer.

755
01:25:53,148 --> 01:25:54,316
You're a God-child?

756
01:25:56,276 --> 01:25:58,111
We do have one thing in common.

757
01:25:59,070 --> 01:26:01,739
Only I don't have 20 or 30 years
left in mine.

758
01:26:01,823 --> 01:26:04,159
Mine is already 10,000 beats overdue.

759
01:26:04,534 --> 01:26:05,785
That's not possible.

760
01:26:06,828 --> 01:26:09,414
You are the authority
on what is not possible.

761
01:26:10,165 --> 01:26:11,333
Aren't you, Irene?

762
01:26:14,002 --> 01:26:16,504
They have got you looking so hard
for any flaw,

763
01:26:17,213 --> 01:26:19,382
that after a while, that's all you see.

764
01:26:22,635 --> 01:26:27,098
For whatever it's worth,
I'm here to tell you that it is possible.

765
01:26:29,100 --> 01:26:30,310
It is possible.

766
01:27:10,058 --> 01:27:12,477
Congratulations, sir. You did it.

767
01:27:13,978 --> 01:27:16,439
His spit was found
in the dead director's eye.

768
01:27:17,065 --> 01:27:18,482
An unaccounted for specimen.

769
01:27:18,566 --> 01:27:20,401
While I was busy obsessing
about an eyelash,

770
01:27:20,485 --> 01:27:22,737
your instincts took us
in the right direction.

771
01:27:23,530 --> 01:27:26,490
So, the invalid had nothing
to do with this?

772
01:27:26,574 --> 01:27:30,119
No, our friend here acted alone.
This mission meant everything to him.

773
01:27:30,203 --> 01:27:31,079
Didn't it?

774
01:27:35,917 --> 01:27:37,835
He knows that if they miss
this launch window,

775
01:27:37,919 --> 01:27:39,619
he won't live to see the next one.

776
01:27:39,754 --> 01:27:44,217
And since nothing can stop the launch now,
he's being very, very cooperative.

777
01:27:48,805 --> 01:27:51,891
So, I imagine you'll be
celebrating tonight, sir?

778
01:27:52,851 --> 01:27:53,726
Of course.

779
01:28:11,369 --> 01:28:12,419
I think she likes us.

780
01:28:13,955 --> 01:28:17,705
Yeah, sure. Just give her a little bit
of time. She'll get used to the idea.

781
01:28:18,251 --> 01:28:19,419
What was he like?

782
01:28:19,794 --> 01:28:21,420
- The cop?
- Yeah.

783
01:28:21,504 --> 01:28:22,338
He was just a cop.

784
01:28:22,422 --> 01:28:23,572
Did you catch his name?

785
01:28:23,840 --> 01:28:25,740
My name was the topic of conversation.

786
01:28:26,176 --> 01:28:28,386
- Well, he'll be back.
- You heard what he said.

787
01:28:28,470 --> 01:28:31,181
- They have their man. It's over.
- No, it's not over.

788
01:28:32,348 --> 01:28:33,349
I have to meet him.

789
01:29:00,376 --> 01:29:01,294
Vincent?

790
01:29:12,180 --> 01:29:13,640
My God, you have changed.

791
01:29:17,852 --> 01:29:20,652
Has it been so long
you don't recognize your own brother?

792
01:29:21,523 --> 01:29:22,690
Are we brothers?

793
01:29:23,358 --> 01:29:25,858
Our parents both died
thinking they'd outlived you.

794
01:29:27,570 --> 01:29:28,821
I had my doubts.

795
01:29:29,697 --> 01:29:32,997
- What are you doing here, Anton?
- I should ask you that question.

796
01:29:33,326 --> 01:29:34,869
I have a right to be here.

797
01:29:35,954 --> 01:29:36,788
You don't.

798
01:29:38,748 --> 01:29:40,875
You almost sound as if you believe that.

799
01:29:42,126 --> 01:29:43,628
I committed no murder.

800
01:29:45,296 --> 01:29:46,631
You must be disappointed.

801
01:29:48,132 --> 01:29:49,551
You committed fraud.

802
01:29:51,511 --> 01:29:54,346
You're in a lot of trouble, Vincent.
I can get you out of here.

803
01:29:54,430 --> 01:29:57,224
Do you have any idea
what it took to get in here?

804
01:29:57,308 --> 01:30:00,008
You've gone as far as you can go.
You come with me now.

805
01:30:00,979 --> 01:30:03,314
There are still a few million miles
left to go.

806
01:30:03,398 --> 01:30:04,231
It's over.

807
01:30:04,315 --> 01:30:07,276
Is that the only way you can succeed,
is to see me fail?

808
01:30:07,360 --> 01:30:08,527
- I'm telling you...
- God!

809
01:30:08,611 --> 01:30:12,115
Even you are going to tell me
what I can and can't do now?

810
01:30:13,908 --> 01:30:17,662
In case you haven't noticed,
I don't need any rescuing.

811
01:30:19,247 --> 01:30:20,540
But you did once.

812
01:30:22,542 --> 01:30:26,462
Well, you've got all the answers.
How do you explain that?

813
01:30:27,130 --> 01:30:29,299
You didn't beat me that day.
I beat myself.

814
01:30:31,009 --> 01:30:32,559
Who are you trying to convince?

815
01:30:33,928 --> 01:30:35,628
Do you want me to prove it to you?

816
01:30:36,139 --> 01:30:40,184
It's not important, Anton. It's forgotten.

817
01:30:41,269 --> 01:30:42,353
I'll prove it to you.

818
01:30:42,895 --> 01:30:45,645
Do you want me to prove it to you?
I'll prove it to you!

819
01:30:46,149 --> 01:30:47,317
I do.

820
01:31:52,840 --> 01:31:53,800
Vincent!

821
01:31:56,052 --> 01:31:56,928
Vincent!

822
01:31:58,846 --> 01:32:00,598
Where's the shore? We're too far out.

823
01:32:00,682 --> 01:32:02,266
- You wanna quit?
- We're too far out.

824
01:32:02,350 --> 01:32:03,476
You wanna quit?

825
01:32:05,353 --> 01:32:06,229
No.

826
01:32:29,502 --> 01:32:30,586
Vincent!

827
01:32:32,422 --> 01:32:34,048
How are you doing this, Vincent?

828
01:32:35,758 --> 01:32:37,258
How have you done any of this?

829
01:32:38,469 --> 01:32:39,845
We have to go back.

830
01:32:39,929 --> 01:32:42,629
It's too late for that.
We're closer to the other side.

831
01:32:43,266 --> 01:32:45,810
What other side?
You want to drown us both?

832
01:32:47,270 --> 01:32:48,770
You want to know how I did it?

833
01:32:49,897 --> 01:32:54,694
This is how I did it.
I never saved anything for the swim back.

834
01:34:39,674 --> 01:34:41,175
You couldn't see, could you?

835
01:34:42,802 --> 01:34:44,554
That night, crossing the street.

836
01:34:46,973 --> 01:34:48,391
You crossed anyway.

837
01:35:04,282 --> 01:35:07,869
If you're still interested, let me know.

838
01:35:15,293 --> 01:35:16,210
Sorry.

839
01:35:21,507 --> 01:35:22,758
The wind caught it.

840
01:36:17,146 --> 01:36:18,746
You're flying today, aren't you?

841
01:36:20,024 --> 01:36:21,567
Look at what a mess you're in.

842
01:36:25,780 --> 01:36:28,491
Come on. I have your samples ready.

843
01:36:30,076 --> 01:36:32,126
I don't need any samples where I'm going.

844
01:36:36,415 --> 01:36:37,815
You might when you get back.

845
01:36:41,796 --> 01:36:44,382
Everything you need
to last you two lifetimes.

846
01:36:48,052 --> 01:36:49,512
Why have you done all this?

847
01:36:50,554 --> 01:36:53,265
So Jerome will always be here
when you need him.

848
01:36:54,100 --> 01:36:57,061
- Where are you going?
- I'm traveling, too.

849
01:37:01,732 --> 01:37:03,232
I don't know how to thank you.

850
01:37:05,820 --> 01:37:06,821
No, no.

851
01:37:07,738 --> 01:37:11,784
I got the better end of the deal.
I only lent you my body.

852
01:37:14,078 --> 01:37:15,454
You lent me your dream.

853
01:37:26,090 --> 01:37:27,591
Not until you're upstairs.

854
01:38:01,959 --> 01:38:02,835
What is this?

855
01:38:03,252 --> 01:38:04,336
New policy.

856
01:38:12,136 --> 01:38:13,387
Flight got you nervous?

857
01:38:14,889 --> 01:38:16,807
Well, there's a problem, Lamar.

858
01:38:17,058 --> 01:38:21,687
I never did tell you about my son, did I?
He's a big fan of yours.

859
01:38:26,317 --> 01:38:31,906
Just remember that I was as good as any
and better than most.

860
01:38:32,573 --> 01:38:34,075
He wants to apply here.

861
01:38:34,742 --> 01:38:38,204
I could have gone up and back,
and nobody would've been the wiser.

862
01:38:38,913 --> 01:38:42,500
Unfortunately,
my son's not all that they promised.

863
01:38:44,126 --> 01:38:46,378
But then, who knows what he could do?

864
01:38:49,131 --> 01:38:50,049
Right?

865
01:39:06,857 --> 01:39:11,946
For future reference, right-handed men
don't hold it with their left.

866
01:39:12,947 --> 01:39:14,615
Just one of those things.

867
01:39:28,129 --> 01:39:30,229
You're going to miss your flight, Vincent.

868
01:42:16,880 --> 01:42:20,884
<i>For someone who was never meant
for this world, I must confess,</i>

869
01:42:21,260 --> 01:42:23,512
<i>I'm suddenly having
a hard time leaving it.</i>

870
01:42:26,390 --> 01:42:29,810
<i>Of course, they say every atom
in our bodies was once part of a star.</i>

871
01:42:31,645 --> 01:42:33,105
<i>Maybe I'm not leaving.</i>

872
01:42:34,815 --> 01:42:36,233
<i>Maybe I'm going home.</i>

